# supabase cli scratch
supabase/.temp/
.env*

# iCloud conflict copies.
#
# This project lives in a synced Desktop folder, so iCloud periodically writes
# "<name> 2.sql" and "<name> 3.sql" next to files it thinks diverged. 216 of
# them accumulated in supabase/migrations and broke the Supabase CLI for
# months, which is why every migration went in by hand through the dashboard.
#
# Ignoring them keeps git clean. It does not stop them appearing, and the CLI
# still chokes on them: `npm run tidy` clears them, and moving this repo out of
# the Desktop is the actual fix.
* 2.*
* 3.*
* [0-9].sql
